		(uuid "5c7b3996-610a-47e3-af94-d1af9cb84640")
	)
	(text "NPN CLASS-A POWER STAGE"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 381 58.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "62630d11-cdd1-4ac6-bd41-25a163fef656")
	)
	(text "ALL FOOTPRINTS UNASSIGNED: exact owned package/lead-form verification required before PCB.\nPins: 2SC5198 / 2SC4793 / 2SA1837 = 1 B, 2 C, 3 E; KSC1845 / KSA992 = 1 E, 2 C, 3 B."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 452.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.25 1.25)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9c76f9f5-ba98-4b1d-9c56-d8d1e16a3334")
	)
	(text "EXTERNAL 40 V SUPPLY / LOCAL DECOUPLING"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 337.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9ed1f8e8-4e0f-487d-809e-ad263bc5b45f")
	)
	(text "RV1 wiper toward SENSE_AVG = minimum current. Set unloaded and current limited.\nSet each R19/R20 to 220 mV (1.00 A each); R21 ~540 mV (2.00 A total).\nI = VBE(Q10) / [alpha x (0.27 + 0.22/2)]; alpha ~0.79 to 1.\nNominal range ~1.6-2.2 A; junction temperature/device spread: TBC.\nR27 pulls Q10 base toward full sense on open wiper: current decreases.\nThermally couple Q10 to lower-bank heatsink; hotter Q10 reduces current.\nQOUT1/2 and QSINK1/2 need substantial external heatsinking and\nelectrical isolation: Toshiba 2SC5198 collector tabs are electrically live.\nMatch parallel devices; each has its own non-inductive 0R22 ballast and 10R stopper."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.22 350.52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.3 1.3)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b0a41de5-8ebf-4da7-932c-d23cfd014d9b")
	)
	(text "CURRENT SINK SETUP / THERMAL"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.22 337.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b7698a0b-54a0-4d11-b34b-884185e65f1e")
	)
	(text "C4: bipolar electrolytic. DC gain = 1.\nAC gain = 1 + 19k/1k = 20 (26 dB).\nQ1/Q2: match VBE and hFE; thermally couple."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 281.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.35 1.35)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bfd9f30a-9410-4e29-8b6a-2924c603c9fc")
	)
	(text "UPPER SIGNAL DRIVER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 294.64 58.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c3c0c28c-b386-4898-a56d-8ea87c448a7d")
	)
	(text "GROUND: one GND net. Separate input/feedback returns from speaker/Zobel and rail-cap returns.\nJoin at J3 GND/local capacitor star. VREF is a quiet signal reference, not a power return."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 403.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.25 1.25)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "daf0a9cf-9538-4593-94a1-511596bcb10b")
	)
	(text "Output-stage idle supply power ~80 W; ~19-20 W per power transistor.\n12 W: 13.86 Vpk / 1.73 Apk. 15 W: 15.49 Vpk / 1.94 Apk.\n2 A sink gives ideal resistive Class-A current ceiling ~16 W / 8 ohm.\nUpper bank peaks ~3.94 A; budget beta=35 => ~113 mA base drive.\nQ8/Q9 require thermal margin; Q6/Q7 ~8 mA, ~0.16 W each at idle.\nC2 100p, C5 DNP, stoppers and L1: bench stability/step response TUNE.\nAMP_OUT ~20 V DC; speaker output AC coupled. Test capacitor charging,\nrail sag, sink transient response and hot DC SOA before PCB layout.\nNo simulation, bench qualification, PSU design or PCB work in this revision."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.22 419.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.25 1.25)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "daf865de-5a94-4808-96c3-90636c6ab249")
	)
	(text "MONO SINGLE-ENDED CLASS-A  |  40 V SINGLE SUPPLY / CAP-COUPLED  |  8 ohm / 12-15 W target"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "df1949d8-cba7-4464-8e13-1852b1472985")
	)
